    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Extract some issues worthy of being flagged to the owner based on this data and make sure not to make-up fake issues if you don't know or can't find worthy issue,\nmain_content : {{ $json.main && $json.main.length > 0 ? $json.main : \"N/A\" }}\nbody : {{ $json.body && $json.body.length > 0 ? $json.body : \"N/A\" }}\nparagraph_text : {{ $json.p && $json.p.length > 0 ? $json.p : \"N/A\" }}\narticle : {{ $json.article && $json.article.length > 0 ? $json.article : \"N/A\" }}\n",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "=I'm one of the founders at Verve Outbound. We're a 2-person B2B SaaS team and we've been doing cold outreach manually, but it doesn't scale and generic \"I saw your profile\" openers get zero replies.\n\nWhat we need: you will be provided with each prospect's company site scrapped data, pulls one real detail worth mentioning, and writes a short opening line referencing it — then queues it into our email sequencer without blasting everything at once and getting us flagged as spam.\n\nIf a prospect's site gives nothing usable, just skip them and tell us why — don't force a fake-sounding line.\n\nOutput Fromat:-\n{\"email\"} : {\"extract the prospect's email from the website to mail him\"}\n{\"email_subject\"} : {\"Subject for the email\"}\n{\"email_body\"} : {\"body of the email\"}\n{\"reason\"} : {\"reason for mentioning\"}\n{\"status\"} : {\"no_worthy_topic\" | \"email_sent\"}"
        }
      },
